    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4d779913",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman with an angry, accusatory expression, pointing directly at the viewer, overlaid with the text 'when you go see your family because of the barbecue.' The scene is designed to humorously convey the frustration or annoyance one might feel when visiting family for a barbecue, implying that the reason for the visit is superficial or obligatory. The intent is to evoke relatable humor about family gatherings, not to target any specific group or individual. While the image uses an exaggerated emotional reaction, it does not contain any abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic content. The humor is situational and self-referential, relying on the universal experience of family obligations, not on harmful stereotypes or protected characteristics. The meme's intent is to entertain through relatable social commentary, not to cause harm or perpetuate discrimination.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_25c0845c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
